          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01WYqh5oCGVo9eqPanzfRWDy",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022pages/concepts/autoscaling.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Autoscaling\\ndescription: Automatically adjusting the number of running replicas of a service based on observed load.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Autoscaling\\n  - tech/Kubernetes\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Two sources; HPA stabilization-window detail confirmed; no formal spec cited.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\nAutoscaling adjusts replica count for a service automatically instead of requiring a\\nhuman to resize it manually. The controller observes some signal \\u2014 CPU/memory\\nutilization, queue depth, or a custom metric \\u2014 and computes a desired replica count on\\nan interval.\\n\\nIn Kubernetes, the **Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA)** polls the metrics API at regular\\nintervals, compares observed metrics against a target, and calculates a desired replica\\ncount. To prevent rapid scaling up and down (flapping), HPA uses a **stabilization\\nwindow** that smooths out temporary spikes or dips in load before triggering a scale\\naction.\\n\\n**Scope distinction:** HPA scales the number of pod replicas running. It does not\\nprovision new cluster nodes \\u2014 that is the responsibility of the **Cluster Autoscaler**,\\na separate controller that runs at the cluster level.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Kubernetes HPA autoscaling mechanism (flapping and stabilization-window detail)\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
      "assistant_text": "Now I\u0027ll update the autoscaling page to add the flapping/stabilization-window detail that the source provides. The source mentions:\n- HPA polls the metrics API on an interval\n- Compares against a target\n- Computes a desired replica count with a stabilization window to avoid flapping\n- HPA does not provision new nodes (Cluster Autoscaler does that)\n\nI\u0027ll integrate this detail into the existing page and update the timestamp and confidence.",
